<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait's NBK 1996 profit up 8.42 percent.</title>
<headline>Kuwait's NBK 1996 profit up 8.42 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>		   (Million dinars unless stated)</p>
<p>				     1996			 1995</p>
<p> Net profit		     68.35			63.05</p>
<p> Net interest income	  88.28			80.69</p>
<p> Net banking income	  114.94		     105.81</p>
<p> Loans and overdrafts    1,529.28		   1,376.56</p>
<p> Government debt bonds     441.98		     498.96</p>
<p> Total assets		3,918.48		   3,871.49</p>
<p> Reserves			212.64		     205.60</p>
<p> Earnings per share (fils)  48.68			44.90</p>
<p> Price earnings ratio (pct) 13.76			12.25</p>
<p>Full Name: National Bank of Kuwait SAK, formed 1952.</p>
<p>Note - These figures were issued by the Kuwait Stock Exchange. There are 1,000 fils to the dinar</p>
<p>($1=0.303 dinar)</p>
</text>
